CLASS com/xk72/proxy/ssl/SSLRecordParser com/xk72/proxy/ssl/SSLRecordParser
	COMMENT a byte-at-a-time TLS record layer parser. It never decrypts: it reads the 5-byte record
	COMMENT header, decides whether the stream even looks like TLS, and reports each record to its
	COMMENT listener. Once change_cipher_spec has gone by, record bodies are reported as encrypted
	COMMENT rather than parsed.
	FIELD field_3793 state Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/SSLRecordParser$State;
	FIELD field_3794 unknownRecordSize J
	FIELD field_3795 handshakeSize J
		COMMENT bytes belonging to change_cipher_spec, alert and handshake records. The stream copiers
		COMMENT subtract this from what they copied so handshake traffic is not counted as body.
	FIELD field_3796 contentType I
		COMMENT 20 change_cipher_spec, 21 alert, 22 handshake, 23 application_data.
	FIELD field_3797 recordLength I
	FIELD field_3798 alertLevel B
	FIELD field_3799 listener Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/class_1395;
	FIELD field_3800 encrypted Z
		COMMENT set at the first change_cipher_spec and never cleared, so everything after it is
		COMMENT reported as an encrypted record.
	FIELD field_3801 handshakeBuffer Ljava/io/ByteArrayOutputStream;
		COMMENT accumulates content-type 22 bodies, since one handshake message can span records.
		COMMENT Charles 4's corpus called this field outputStream.
	FIELD field_3802 recordBytesRead I
	FIELD field_3803 alertDescription B
	FIELD field_3804 applicationDataSize J
		COMMENT also accumulates everything read after the stream turns out not to be TLS.
	FIELD field_3805 versionMinor I
	FIELD field_3806 versionMajor I
	METHOD <init> (Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/class_1395;)V
		ARG 1 listener
	METHOD method_3794 isPlausibleRecord ()Z
		COMMENT [inferred] the check that decides whether this is TLS at all: a known content type,
		COMMENT major version 3, minor 0-4, and a length within the 32KB record limit. Failing it puts
		COMMENT the parser into its terminal not-SSL state for the rest of the stream.
	METHOD method_3795 getHandshakeSize ()J
	METHOD method_3796 parseHeaderByte (B)V
		COMMENT [inferred] advances the header state machine one byte: content type, major, minor, then
		COMMENT the two length bytes.
		ARG 1 b
	METHOD method_3797 write (I)V
		ARG 1 b
	METHOD method_3798 write ([BII)V
		ARG 1 buffer
		ARG 2 offset
		ARG 3 length
	METHOD method_3799 endOfRecord ()V
		COMMENT [inferred] dispatches the finished record to the listener by content type.
	CLASS State State
